Z||000000||My7Fieros||01-13-2001||06:49 PM||||Just courious, what is "bitrate" and "ping"..does it make any difference when downloading? (Im a 56k...zzzzz lol)||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||01-13-2001||06:52 PM||||i've downloaded a bunch of songs with both of those. downloaded the same. not really sure if one is faster or whatever. but it still worked either way.||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||01-13-2001||07:04 PM||||It is the quality of the song. A low bit rate (eg. 64) is of lower quality than a high quality (eg. 192) recording. Lower bitrate files are smaller file size, and will download quicker and take up less space. Most of the mp3s I download are 128, which I find to be a good compromise between quality and file size.||||reg||1
