Z||000006||RNGCRSH||01-14-2001||11:37 PM||||Bitrate is the way the song was encoded the higher the bitrate the larger the song and the better the quality.<P>The ping number you see is the round trip time for a data packet to travel between the napster server and the person who has the songs stored on there computer.<P>If you are downloading your ping time to the person with the files will be your napster ping plus theirs. The higher the number the slower the conection, but with a 56k modem it really doesn't matter. Try to only down load from dsl and above and you will do better.<p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||1
